# ROE ticket flow

Agents follow this sequence for every new ROE ticket **without the user restating it**. Skip a step only if the user explicitly says so (e.g. “docs-only” or “hotfix”).

## Naming (required)

| Surface | Format |
|---------|--------|
| Issue / PR | `[ROE-NNN] Short title (ABC-NNN)` — omit `(ABC-NNN)` if no workstream alias |
| Commit | `[ROE-NNN][ABC-NNN] imperative message` — or `[ROE-NNN] message` if no alias |
| Branch | `feature/ROE-NNN-kebab-slug` from fresh `origin/develop` |

**ROE-NNN** is the global serial (never skip). Next free is tracked in `project.md` / `.lovable/plan.md`.

## Sequence

1. **Audit** — Read CONTEXT_PLAN (+ CURSOR.md if touching `src/` or `supabase/`). Search before inventing. Prefer a canvas for multi-finding audits.
2. **Impact analysis** — Write `docs/ROE-NNN-*-impact-analysis.md` (problem, acceptance, scope, files, test plan, **deploy/ops**). Await user approval before coding unless they already said “implement”.
3. **Branch** — `git fetch origin develop && git checkout -b feature/ROE-NNN-… origin/develop`
4. **Implement** — Minimal diff; honor sync pairs; add/adjust Vitest for scoring/dietary/intent/pairings.
5. **Ask label chips (when applicable)** — If the ticket adds or changes **user-discoverable Ask capability** (new intent enums, situational modes, dietary/wellness/lens paths, cuisine modes, etc.), either:
   - **Same PR:** update `src/pages/Ask.tsx` `EXAMPLES` (“Or try” chips) + placeholder so chips teach the new capability, **or**
   - **Explicit follow-up:** queue the next ROE (e.g. ASK-00N) in `TODO.md` / `.lovable/plan.md` / impact §Out of scope — do **not** silently ship engine-only discovery gaps.
6. **Docs sync** — Same PR: `TODO.md`, `.lovable/plan.md`, `.cursor/CONTEXT_PLAN.md`, relevant CURSOR.md, next-free ROE bump.
7. **Ship** — Commit → push → `gh pr create` (title matches issue) → add to Rasaoi QA Board → set **In progress**.
8. **Ops / deploy** — In the PR body, state exactly what is required after merge:
   - Frontend: Vercel auto-deploy on `develop` / `main` (note if none).
   - Edge: `npx supabase functions deploy <name> --no-verify-jwt` for each touched function (often `parse-intent`; also `estimate-glycemic` / others when changed). Prefer `npm run supabase:deploy:all` only when multiple functions need refresh.
   - DB: `npm run supabase:db:push` (or documented migration apply) when migrations land; regenerate `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` if schema changed.
   - Culinary index: `node scripts/personal/build-culinary-index.mjs` when matrix/registry sources change (commit rebuilt `src/data/culinary-index.json` in that PR).
9. **QA closeout** — After merge: run noted ops; board → **QA**; stakeholder Pass → **Done**.

## Do not

- Commit secrets or `supabase/.temp/*`
- Skip impact analysis for non-trivial product changes
- Invent APIs/tables not in CONTEXT_PLAN without searching first
- Use `IP-FIX` / `FUL` / `ASK` as the sole ID — always assign **ROE-NNN** and append alias
- Ship new Ask-parse capability without either chip updates or a queued chip follow-up ROE
